% References for the JOSS submission draft (paper/paper.md).
%
% AUDITED 2026-08-28 against primary metadata. "Well known" is not "checked",
% and checking found three defects in this file alone:
%
%   nistairmf   - repeated `institution =`; bibtex keeps the first and silently
%                 drops the rest, so a malformed entry never announces itself.
%   openlineage - title was "An open standard for lineage metadata collection";
%                 the project's own tagline is "An open framework for data
%                 lineage collection and analysis". Author now names the
%                 governing body (LF AI & Data Foundation), not "Contributors".
%   euaiact     - a regulation has two dates; the adoption (13 Jun 2024) and
%                 Official Journal publication (12 Jul 2024) are now both given.
%
% Confirmed unchanged: intoto (USENIX Security '19, pp. 1393-1410), rfc3161,
% rfc8785, provo, opentelemetry (living spec, no tagged releases).
%
% NOTE: usenix.org and dl.acm.org return HTTP 403 to automated fetches. Those
% were confirmed via dblp and Crossref instead - do not re-hit that wall.
%
% This file and papers/systems-2026/refs.bib cite seven references in common.
% Style may differ between the two venues; a FACT may not. A guard now fails if
% year/doi/pages/volume/number disagree across them, or if any entry repeats a
% field - opentelemetry carried year=2024 in one and 2026 in the other, for the
% same URL, and nothing was looking.

